  OFFER WINDOWS AND THE CART DELIVERY BAR, 7 Nov 2026, Part 2a.
  TL.offer(t) says which offer window t is in: 'early', 'bf' or ''.
  TL.deliveryTotal(cart) is the basket figure the cart's free-delivery bar and
  its "Delivery is free with this" row compare with £100. Outside the windows
  it is cart.total_price, as before. Inside them it is
  cart.original_total_price, the full price, because Shopify takes automatic
  discounts and codes applied by link out of total_price, so a £100 basket
  would read £85 and the bar would say it was short while checkout ships it
  free. At 15% the full price at £100 matches checkout's rule exactly. In
  early access a basket of £85 to £99.99 with no code ships free at checkout
  while the bar says it is short. That errs in the customer's favour.
  Both snippets ask this one helper: snippets/tl-delivery-summary.liquid and
  snippets/tl-cart-recommend.liquid.

  COUNTING: days are calendar days in UK time, today included, so on Monday
  14 December it reads 3 days left (14, 15, 16). In the last 48 hours it
  counts hours, rounded up. On the deadline's own day it says Last day.

  CHECKING A DATE ON A COPY, 9 Nov 2026. On any theme that is not the live
  one, ?tl_now=2026-11-28T10:00:00Z on the address sets the clock for that
  page, so every timed line, countdown and price can be looked at for any
  moment before it comes. TL.now() returns the set time, and every snippet
  asks TL.now(). The live theme never carries the hook: theme.role is
  'main' there, so the lines below are not rendered at all. The server-side
  gates in tl-urgency and tl-buybox open fully on a copy for the same reason,
  so the script here is the only judge of what shows. A copy is for looking,
  never for buying.

  CROSSED-OUT PRICES, his word of 8 Nov 2026, "crossed out prices do like
  ezra suggested", confirmed 10 Nov ("Crossed out stands"). In the weekend
  window only, the buy box, the product cards (collections, search, the
  shelves) and the cart's recommendations show the price after the cut in
  green with the shop price struck through beside it. The theme works it
  out from the live price and the depth setting (settings.tl_bf_depth),
  behind the switch settings.tl_bf_price, on by default since 10 Nov on his
  word. No compare-at price is ever set, so nothing reaches the Google feed
  and nothing is left behind after Thu 3 Dec.
  TL.bfDepth(t) is the depth in force at t, or 0. TL.bfPay(cents, t) is the
  price after the cut, the cut rounded down to the penny as Shopify does it
  (read from a draft order calculation, 10 Nov 2026).
  The html class tl-bf-price is set while it is in force; the cards show
  their green price under that class and their plain price without it.
  Early access shows no crossed-out price: only a code holder gets the cut.
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign tl_bfp_d = 0
  if settings.tl_bf_price or theme.role != 'main'
    if settings.tl_bf_depth != blank
      assign tl_bfp_d = settings.tl_bf_depth | plus: 0
    endif
  endif
  assign tl_bfp_int = tl_bfp_d | floor
  if tl_bfp_int != tl_bfp_d or tl_bfp_d < 1 or tl_bfp_d > 99
    assign tl_bfp_d = 0
  endif
-%}
<script>
  (function () {
    if (window.TL) return;
    var BFD = {{ tl_bfp_d | json }};
    var D = {
      eaStart: Date.UTC(2026, 10, 20, 0, 0, 0),
      eaEnd: Date.UTC(2026, 10, 23, 23, 59, 59),
      bfTeaser: Date.UTC(2026, 10, 24, 0, 0, 0),
      bfStart: Date.UTC(2026, 10, 27, 0, 0, 0),
      bfEnd: Date.UTC(2026, 11, 3, 23, 59, 59),
      xmasEnd: Date.UTC(2026, 11, 16, 23, 59, 59),
      giftEnd: Date.UTC(2026, 11, 24, 23, 59, 59)
    };
    var DAY = 86400000, HOUR = 3600000;
    var fixed = null;
    {%- if theme.role != 'main' %}
    try {
      var q = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('tl_now');
      if (q) { var f = Date.parse(q); if (!isNaN(f)) fixed = f; }
    } catch (e) {}
    {%- endif %}
    function now() { return fixed == null ? Date.now() : fixed; }
    function ukDate(t) { return new Date(t).toISOString().slice(0, 10); }
    function dayNumber(t) { return Math.floor(Date.parse(ukDate(t) + 'T00:00:00Z') / DAY); }
    function plural(n, w) { return n + ' ' + w + (n === 1 ? '' : 's'); }
    function phase(t) {
      return {
        ea: t >= D.eaStart && t <= D.eaEnd,
        bfTeaser: t >= D.bfTeaser && t < D.bfStart,
        bfLive: t >= D.bfStart && t <= D.bfEnd,
        xmas: t <= D.xmasEnd,
        gift: t > D.xmasEnd && t <= D.giftEnd
      };
    }
    function left(end, t) {
      var ms = end - t;
      if (ms <= 0) return null;
      var hours = Math.ceil(ms / HOUR);
      if (ukDate(t) === ukDate(end)) return { kind: 'lastday', n: hours };
      if (ms <= 48 * HOUR) return { kind: 'hours', n: hours };
      return { kind: 'days', n: dayNumber(end) - dayNumber(t) + 1 };
    }
    function offer(t) {
      if (t >= D.eaStart && t <= D.eaEnd) return 'early';
      if (t >= D.bfStart && t <= D.bfEnd) return 'bf';
      return '';
    }
    function deliveryTotal(cart, t) {
      if (!cart) return 0;
      var paid = cart.total_price || 0;
      if (!offer(t == null ? now() : t)) return paid;
      var full = cart.original_total_price;
      return typeof full === 'number' ? full : paid;
    }
    function bfDepth(t) {
      return BFD && offer(t == null ? now() : t) === 'bf' ? BFD : 0;
    }
    function bfPay(cents, t) {
      var d = bfDepth(t);
      return d ? cents - Math.floor(cents * d / 100 + 1e-6) : cents;
    }
    var BF = '15% off every bottle, case and set';
    var texts = {
      xmasCount: function (t) {
        var l = left(D.xmasEnd, t);
        if (!l) return '';
        if (l.kind === 'lastday') return 'Last day to order for Christmas. ' + plural(l.n, 'hour') + ' left.';
        return plural(l.n, l.kind === 'hours' ? 'hour' : 'day') + ' left to order for Christmas.';
      },
      xmasLine: function (t) {
        var l = left(D.xmasEnd, t);
        if (!l) return '';
        var tail = l.kind === 'lastday' ? 'Last day, ' + plural(l.n, 'hour') + ' left.' : plural(l.n, l.kind === 'hours' ? 'hour' : 'day') + ' left.';
        return 'Order by Wednesday 16 December for Christmas delivery. ' + tail;
      },
      ea: function (t) {
        return phase(t).ea ? 'Early access is open. Join the list and we email you a code straight away.' : '';
      },
      bf: function (t) {
        var p = phase(t);
        if (p.bfTeaser) return 'Black Friday starts Friday. Every bottle, case and set.';
        if (!p.bfLive) return '';
        var l = left(D.bfEnd, t);
        if (!l) return '';
        if (l.kind === 'lastday') return 'Last day of Black Friday: ' + BF + '. ' + plural(l.n, 'hour') + ' left.';
        return 'Black Friday: ' + BF + '. ' + plural(l.n, l.kind === 'hours' ? 'hour' : 'day') + ' left.';
      },
      gift: function (t) {
        return phase(t).gift ? 'Too late for Christmas delivery? A gift card comes by email, straight away.' : '';
      }
    };
    var t0 = now();
    var p0 = phase(t0);
    var root = document.documentElement;
    if (p0.ea) root.classList.add('tl-ea');
    if (p0.bfTeaser) root.classList.add('tl-bf-teaser');
    if (p0.bfLive) root.classList.add('tl-bf-live');
    if (!p0.xmas) root.classList.add('tl-xmas-over');
    if (p0.gift) root.classList.add('tl-gift');
    if (bfDepth(t0)) root.classList.add('tl-bf-price');
    window.TL = { dates: D, phase: phase, offer: offer, deliveryTotal: deliveryTotal, left: left, texts: texts, bfDepth: bfDepth, bfPay: bfPay, now: now, pinned: fixed != null };
  })();
</script>
<style>
  html.tl-bf-live .tl-six-timed,
  html.tl-xmas-over .tl-six-timed { display: none !important; }
  [data-tl-fill]:empty { display: none; }
  /* Crossed-out prices: the card's own price shows unless tl-bf-price is set. */
  .tl-cw { display: none; }
  html.tl-bf-price .tl-cw { display: inline; }
  html.tl-bf-price [data-tl-cw-alt] { display: none !important; }
  .tl-cw__now { color: #1f7a3a; font-weight: 700; margin-right: 6px; }
  .tl-was { color: #5c5a57; font-weight: 400; text-decoration: line-through; text-decoration-thickness: 1px; }
  /* Belt and braces: a line outside its window stays hidden even where a
     re-rendered fragment did not run its script. */
  html:not(.tl-ea) [data-tl-fill="ea"],
  html:not(.tl-bf-live):not(.tl-bf-teaser) [data-tl-fill="bf"],
  html.tl-xmas-over [data-tl-fill="xmasLine"],
  html.tl-xmas-over [data-tl-fill="xmasCount"],
  html:not(.tl-gift) [data-tl-fill="gift"] { display: none !important; }
</style>
{%- comment -%}
  EARLY BIRD BAND, 9 Nov 2026, from the design of 9 November, board 1.
  The homepage band "Shop it first." shows from the day the early bird page
  goes live until the end of Monday 23 November UK, then hides.
  · The start is the page itself: sections/tl-early-bird-band.liquid renders
    only while /pages/early-bird is published, so the band never links to a
    page nobody can open. No start date to keep in step.
  · The end is ebBandEnd below, the one date for the band. Change it here
    only on his word.
  TL.earlyBand(t) is true while t is inside the window. The html class
  tl-eb-band is set while it is, and the band is hidden without it, so a
  cached page or a fragment that missed its script never shows it late.
  Kept as its own block so it reads beside the other dates without touching
  the lines above.

  EARLY ACCESS OPEN, his word of 9 Nov 2026: from Fri 20 Nov 00:00 to Mon
  23 Nov 23:59:59 UK the early bird page and its thank-you page change their
  words, because late joiners get their code straight away. TL.earlyOpen(t)
  is true inside that window and sets the html class tl-eb-open; the pages
  show their "open" words under that class (snippets/tl-eb-style). It reads
  TL.dates.eaStart and eaEnd, the early access window, which the D list
  above holds since the cart fix merged; the fallback below only runs if
  they are ever missing, so there is still one place to change them.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script>
  (function () {
    if (!window.TL || window.TL.earlyBand) return;
    TL.dates.ebBandEnd = Date.UTC(2026, 10, 23, 23, 59, 59);
    TL.earlyBand = function (t) { return (t == null ? TL.now() : t) <= TL.dates.ebBandEnd; };
    if (!TL.dates.eaStart) {
      TL.dates.eaStart = Date.UTC(2026, 10, 20, 0, 0, 0);
      TL.dates.eaEnd = Date.UTC(2026, 10, 23, 23, 59, 59);
    }
    TL.earlyOpen = function (t) { var n = t == null ? TL.now() : t; return n >= TL.dates.eaStart && n <= TL.dates.eaEnd; };
    var root = document.documentElement;
    if (TL.earlyBand(TL.now())) root.classList.add('tl-eb-band');
    if (TL.earlyOpen(TL.now())) root.classList.add('tl-eb-open');
  })();
</script>
<style>
  .tl-ebb { display: none; }
  html.tl-eb-band .tl-ebb { display: block; }
</style>
